WEBVTT

00:00:11.470 --> 00:00:13.490
She's sleeping soundly.

00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:17.490
It's about time for you to wake up!

00:00:18.040 --> 00:00:20.680
After all, today's career counseling day.

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:29.760
Good morning, honey.

00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:30.760
Now then...

00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:44.830
Great. It looks like Yuko's in 
good spirits as usual today.

00:00:44.830 --> 00:00:46.280
Another gold star.

00:01:04.420 --> 00:01:06.420
Goodness. Was that a bird?

00:01:10.360 --> 00:01:14.550
Goodness gracious, I'm happy to 
see you've come to play with me.

00:01:18.050 --> 00:01:19.930
<i>This is bad! She'll find me!</i>

00:01:19.930 --> 00:01:21.360
Goodness.

00:01:23.430 --> 00:01:24.850
Lion-chan

00:01:25.890 --> 00:01:28.100
Hello? Lion-chan?

00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:29.610
Lion-chan?

00:01:29.610 --> 00:01:34.420
No, Lion! Don't go!

00:01:30.470 --> 00:01:32.940
Yuko-senpai! How are you doing?

00:01:33.940 --> 00:01:36.420
<i>Pudding? Do you want to eat some pudding?</i>

00:01:36.420 --> 00:01:37.660
How are you doing!

00:01:37.660 --> 00:01:39.840
Oh, I'm doing well.

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:41.020
How about you?

00:01:41.020 --> 00:01:42.330
<i>I'm doing well!</i>

00:01:42.330 --> 00:01:44.450
<i>I'm coming back to the dorm tomorrow.</i>

00:01:44.450 --> 00:01:46.190
Goodness, are you?

00:01:46.190 --> 00:01:48.280
Be careful on your way back.

00:01:50.240 --> 00:01:52.840
A smile definitely suits you best.

00:01:57.720 --> 00:01:59.020
Yuko!

00:03:34.550 --> 00:03:35.840
Morigaya-san.

00:03:36.760 --> 00:03:37.730
Coming.

00:03:37.730 --> 00:03:42.740
6th Year Career Counseling in Progress

00:03:38.800 --> 00:03:40.260
Excuse me.

00:03:43.970 --> 00:03:45.510
Yuko!

00:03:46.800 --> 00:03:47.930
Yuko.

00:03:49.070 --> 00:03:50.540
Sorry for making you wait.

00:03:51.160 --> 00:03:53.640
Well then, shall we head into town?

00:03:53.640 --> 00:03:56.340
Wait a moment. The president isn't here yet.

00:03:56.630 --> 00:03:58.670
Now that you mention it, she isn't.

00:03:58.670 --> 00:04:00.800
She's usually so punctual.

00:04:01.150 --> 00:04:02.960
I wonder if anything happened to her.

00:04:03.700 --> 00:04:05.510
Sorry for making you wait, honey.

00:04:11.700 --> 00:04:15.750
We had career counseling 
today too, didn't we?

00:04:15.750 --> 00:04:16.670
Yeah.

00:04:16.670 --> 00:04:18.400
Aoi-san, how did yours go?

00:04:18.720 --> 00:04:21.410
I'm going to go back to the 
same office I used to work in.

00:04:21.410 --> 00:04:22.500
How about you, Yuko?

00:04:24.590 --> 00:04:27.610
I still haven't decided.

00:04:27.610 --> 00:04:29.330
You're not going to join ALCA?

00:04:29.860 --> 00:04:31.730
How do I put it into words?

00:04:31.730 --> 00:04:35.330
I only formed my covenant towards the 
latter half of my time at the academy.

00:04:35.860 --> 00:04:38.400
Not only that, when I think about it...

00:04:39.570 --> 00:04:42.790
I'm a little afraid of fighting.

00:04:43.530 --> 00:04:46.340
I'm sorry. I know I shouldn't be saying this.

00:04:47.220 --> 00:04:49.640
You're going to graduate in 6 months.

00:04:49.640 --> 00:04:51.350
Are you still undecided 
about what you want to do?

00:04:52.130 --> 00:04:53.460
You're such an excellent student.

00:04:53.460 --> 00:04:56.350
I was sure you'd go on to 
join ALCA as a Logicalist

00:04:56.350 --> 00:04:59.170
and show everyone just how capable you are.

00:04:59.680 --> 00:05:02.870
There are offices that have already 
expressed interest in you joining them.

00:05:02.870 --> 00:05:04.360
Yes, but...

00:05:05.270 --> 00:05:07.910
Do you have another career path in mind?

00:05:10.650 --> 00:05:13.280
ALCA isn't your only option.

00:05:13.280 --> 00:05:16.980
We also have students who are aiming 
to attend regular universities.

00:05:16.980 --> 00:05:20.440
But those are students that 
have yet to form a covenant.

00:05:20.440 --> 00:05:23.950
Morigaya-san has some of the best grades
in the S-Class.

00:05:23.950 --> 00:05:27.630
Even if the world is at peace 
now, she's got so much potential.

00:05:27.630 --> 00:05:29.460
Um, I...

00:05:30.180 --> 00:05:32.860
No... It's nothing.

00:05:32.860 --> 00:05:34.780
Feel free to speak your mind.

00:05:34.780 --> 00:05:37.970
Your future belongs to you.

00:05:37.970 --> 00:05:39.580
We're happy if you join ALCA.

00:05:39.580 --> 00:05:41.630
We're happy if you go to a university.

00:05:41.630 --> 00:05:43.100
And we're happy if you go out and find a job.

00:05:43.600 --> 00:05:45.400
There are lots of paths open to you.

00:05:46.030 --> 00:05:48.240
Housewife Letter 
of Recommendation

00:05:46.030 --> 00:05:48.240
Morigaya

00:05:48.800 --> 00:05:53.060
In any event, now is the time 
to carefully think things over.

00:05:53.660 --> 00:05:55.330
I'll always be here to talk with you.

00:05:55.610 --> 00:05:58.470
Right. Thank you very much.

00:06:00.220 --> 00:06:01.970
Yuko-san, what's the matter?

00:06:01.970 --> 00:06:03.840
You still have half a year left,

00:06:03.840 --> 00:06:05.840
so you'll be better off 
taking the time to think.

00:06:05.840 --> 00:06:09.180
Aoi, Ashley-chan, thank you.

00:06:09.620 --> 00:06:10.840
Mizuki, what are you going to do?

00:06:11.900 --> 00:06:13.590
Well isn't this unusual.

00:06:13.590 --> 00:06:15.850
You don't usually take interest in me.

00:06:16.330 --> 00:06:18.230
If you don't want to share, that's fine by—

00:06:18.230 --> 00:06:21.820
If you want to know that badly, 
I'll tell you as a special favor.

00:06:21.970 --> 00:06:23.120
I've nothing to hide.

00:06:23.120 --> 00:06:26.720
After all, my plans are quite large in scale.

00:06:26.720 --> 00:06:27.780
Large in scale?

00:06:30.160 --> 00:06:31.910
A grand revolution at ALCA.

00:06:36.020 --> 00:06:38.710
Let's work hard on our school 
festival preparations.

00:06:38.710 --> 00:06:39.420
Of course.

00:06:39.420 --> 00:06:40.290
Yeah.

00:06:40.290 --> 00:06:42.090
Don't pretend you didn't hear me!

00:06:42.290 --> 00:06:45.050
And what exactly is this grand revolution?

00:06:46.680 --> 00:06:50.550
It's because the world is so peaceful 
now that I feel danger lurks.

00:06:51.100 --> 00:06:51.800
Huh?

00:06:52.080 --> 00:06:57.020
In the past, we all faced a mutual threat 
of invasion from alternate worlds.

00:06:57.020 --> 00:06:58.840
Thanks to that, the world 
banded together as one.

00:06:59.550 --> 00:07:00.810
But that's not the case any longer.

00:07:01.170 --> 00:07:03.410
If we go off track just a bit,

00:07:03.410 --> 00:07:06.440
it could spell the beginning of 
humanity fighting among ourselves.

00:07:06.440 --> 00:07:08.070
That's what I'm afraid of.

00:07:08.600 --> 00:07:09.540
If it comes to that,

00:07:09.540 --> 00:07:14.350
Logicalists, who have such strong powers, 
will most certainly be dragged into it.

00:07:16.300 --> 00:07:17.960
That's when it came to me.

00:07:18.690 --> 00:07:22.220
ALCA should put all of its efforts 
into functioning as a system

00:07:22.220 --> 00:07:25.340
that exists to maintain balance 
everywhere in the world.

00:07:25.340 --> 00:07:27.340
That's my dream for the future.

00:07:27.890 --> 00:07:29.630
Th-That certainly is grand.

00:07:30.170 --> 00:07:34.130
Dreams are only worth chasing 
because they're so hard to attain.

00:07:34.130 --> 00:07:36.650
Th-The president is actually taking 
this conversation seriously.

00:07:36.650 --> 00:07:38.690
Please, come back to us.

00:07:38.690 --> 00:07:40.210
Wait, wait, wait.

00:07:40.210 --> 00:07:42.460
I'm actually pretty serious normally!

00:07:44.520 --> 00:07:46.120
Why are you laughing?!

00:07:52.100 --> 00:07:53.820
<i>My dreams for the future, huh?</i>

00:07:54.590 --> 00:07:56.070
<i>Up until a little while ago,</i>

00:07:56.070 --> 00:07:58.760
<i>I thought I had no choice but to join ALCA.</i>

00:07:59.670 --> 00:08:00.600
<i>But...</i>

00:08:02.680 --> 00:08:06.470
<i>When I was little, I wanted 
to be a patisserie.</i>

00:08:07.670 --> 00:08:10.000
<i>I also wanted to be a florist.</i>

00:08:10.000 --> 00:08:12.650
<i>Even an idol at one point.</i>

00:08:13.520 --> 00:08:17.470
<i>Back then, I was overflowing with dreams.</i>

00:08:18.020 --> 00:08:19.760
Huh? What happened to Yuko?

00:08:22.050 --> 00:08:24.480
Yuko. What's the matter?

00:08:39.690 --> 00:08:40.920
Coming.

00:08:44.900 --> 00:08:45.620
Goodness.

00:08:45.620 --> 00:08:47.740
High Grade

00:08:45.620 --> 00:08:47.740
Long lasting!!

00:08:45.620 --> 00:08:47.740
Bright!!

00:08:46.640 --> 00:08:48.010
Hey.

00:08:48.010 --> 00:08:50.650
How about we take a trip 
back to our childhood?

00:08:54.490 --> 00:08:58.010
How many years has it been since 
we've lit fireworks together?

00:08:58.010 --> 00:08:59.830
Not since we were kids.

00:08:59.830 --> 00:09:01.990
So around 12 or 13 years ago, I suppose.

00:09:01.990 --> 00:09:04.670
Wrong! That can't be right.

00:09:04.670 --> 00:09:07.170
Didn't we do it a little 
before entering the academy?

00:09:07.170 --> 00:09:08.400
Did we?

00:09:09.400 --> 00:09:11.120
Well, in any event.

00:09:11.120 --> 00:09:13.800
You and I have a lot of history together.

00:09:15.000 --> 00:09:18.750
We were always in the same class 
since kindergarten, after all.

00:09:18.750 --> 00:09:20.290
That's true.

00:09:20.290 --> 00:09:22.540
Right up until you formed your covenant.

00:09:23.890 --> 00:09:25.880
I'd expect nothing less of you.

00:09:26.550 --> 00:09:29.760
No. My power is nothing special.

00:09:31.810 --> 00:09:33.990
It's not well-suited for battle.

00:09:34.530 --> 00:09:36.300
That's not true.

00:09:36.930 --> 00:09:39.050
You have an amazing power.

00:09:39.650 --> 00:09:41.530
You should feel proud.

00:09:41.530 --> 00:09:42.600
Mizuki...

00:09:43.170 --> 00:09:47.840
On the other hand, I couldn't 
even form a covenant.

00:09:47.840 --> 00:09:50.460
Honestly, I did 
find it very frustrating.

00:09:50.460 --> 00:09:53.870
But now I feel it's thanks to that that 
I'm able to see the world the way I do,

00:09:53.870 --> 00:09:56.030
and I'm proud of that.

00:09:59.850 --> 00:10:01.780
You're amazing, Mizuki.

00:10:01.780 --> 00:10:03.800
Wha? I am?

00:10:03.800 --> 00:10:07.290
Well, you've already got your goals in sight

00:10:07.290 --> 00:10:09.790
and you know where your prospects lie.

00:10:10.470 --> 00:10:15.650
In contrast, I still haven't 
even found a dream for myself.

00:10:17.820 --> 00:10:20.680
I wonder what I'm supposed 
to do with my life?

00:10:20.680 --> 00:10:22.010
What you're supposed to do?

00:10:22.010 --> 00:10:23.570
You mean what you want to do.

00:10:25.250 --> 00:10:28.930
It's no fun if you think about 
your future as some kind of duty

00:10:28.930 --> 00:10:31.060
like you're supposed to work in 
one career, and follow one path.

00:10:31.640 --> 00:10:35.610
I think you're better off thinking about what 
you want, and what you want to do.

00:10:35.610 --> 00:10:39.500
There's no better motivation 
than what you like.

00:10:40.610 --> 00:10:42.590
What I like?

00:10:44.110 --> 00:10:46.830
U-Uh, Yuko.

00:10:46.830 --> 00:10:49.310
Putting thought into it is important, 
but as a change of pace?

00:10:49.310 --> 00:10:49.750
Here.

00:10:50.880 --> 00:10:52.500
A Bon Dance competition?

00:10:53.040 --> 00:10:57.160
Y-Yuko, will you make my dreams come true?

00:10:57.160 --> 00:10:57.510
Huh?

00:10:58.490 --> 00:11:02.480
J-Just you and me, on a yukata date—

00:11:02.480 --> 00:11:04.900
Yuko-senpai!

00:11:05.810 --> 00:11:07.240
Goodness gracious.

00:11:07.240 --> 00:11:08.550
I thought you were arriving tomorrow.

00:11:08.550 --> 00:11:11.310
But I wanted to see you as fast as I could.

00:11:11.860 --> 00:11:13.350
Welcome home.

00:11:13.350 --> 00:11:14.980
You came back at the perfect time.

00:11:14.980 --> 00:11:18.320
It turns out there's going to be 
a Bon Dance competition tomorrow.

00:11:18.730 --> 00:11:20.320
Let's invite everyone.

00:11:20.320 --> 00:11:21.380
Yay!

00:11:21.380 --> 00:11:25.690
Yuko, don't go!

00:11:24.370 --> 00:11:26.950
Episode 7 
Even Presidents Fall From Trees

00:11:28.520 --> 00:11:30.270
Unless you've finished your homework,

00:11:29.830 --> 00:11:32.330
<b>6 Hours Until Bon Dance!!</b>

00:11:30.270 --> 00:11:33.200
your Bon Dance will never begin.

00:11:33.760 --> 00:11:35.400
Yeah.

00:11:35.400 --> 00:11:37.500
Gosh! Where's your spirit?

00:11:37.940 --> 00:11:39.260
Yeah.

00:11:40.020 --> 00:11:42.600
And we still have to prepare 
for the school festival.

00:11:42.760 --> 00:11:45.200
You can do that after you take
 care of what you need to do first.

00:11:45.220 --> 00:11:45.670
Yeah baby!

00:11:46.720 --> 00:11:49.270
Why isn't Lion over here with us?

00:11:49.760 --> 00:11:52.220
'Cause I've already done my homework.

00:11:52.220 --> 00:11:53.770
It was tough.

00:11:53.770 --> 00:11:55.520
<i>You're not going anywhere.</i>

00:11:55.860 --> 00:11:56.730
Goodness gracious.

00:11:57.090 --> 00:11:58.730
You're sure giving it your all.

00:11:59.160 --> 00:12:01.920
How about you take a little break with lunch?

00:12:01.920 --> 00:12:02.610
Here.

00:12:04.080 --> 00:12:05.030
Yuko-senpai.

00:12:05.030 --> 00:12:06.980
I'm most grateful for your concern.

00:12:06.980 --> 00:12:09.910
I'll take responsibility for the food and 
make sure everything's taken care of.

00:12:09.910 --> 00:12:12.510
You can have one rice ball after 
finishing one book of drills.

00:12:12.510 --> 00:12:15.650
I can't wait that long! I can't! No!

00:12:15.650 --> 00:12:18.480
Yuko-senpai, what did you use 
as the filling for these rice balls?

00:12:18.480 --> 00:12:20.380
Um, well...

00:12:24.960 --> 00:12:26.010
Nina-chan!

00:12:27.470 --> 00:12:29.160
What are you doing?

00:12:29.160 --> 00:12:31.020
This? The Bon Dance.

00:12:31.690 --> 00:12:33.640
Daddy taught me.

00:12:35.940 --> 00:12:37.650
Nina-chan?

00:12:37.650 --> 00:12:40.650
I don't think that's the Bon Dance.

00:12:46.240 --> 00:12:47.990
I'm done.

00:12:47.990 --> 00:12:50.430
Here. You really pulled through, Mahiro-chan.

00:12:50.850 --> 00:12:52.860
You really gave it your all, Mahiro-chan.

00:12:52.860 --> 00:12:54.820
I'm gonna take a break.

00:12:54.820 --> 00:12:56.130
Good job.

00:12:56.130 --> 00:12:58.360
It looks like we'll be 
done over here soon too.

00:12:59.170 --> 00:13:00.630
Well then, Lion-chan.

00:13:00.630 --> 00:13:02.340
Should we go ahead and get changed first?

00:13:07.520 --> 00:13:11.430
Yuko-senpai, Lion-san, the flower 
patterns on your yukatas are lovely.

00:13:11.860 --> 00:13:13.100
Yup.

00:13:13.590 --> 00:13:15.810
Yeah. They're cute.

00:13:16.290 --> 00:13:18.520
Your bunnies are cute, too!

00:13:19.950 --> 00:13:23.370
Speaking of, who do you think's gonna win?

00:13:23.370 --> 00:13:24.280
Win?

00:13:24.280 --> 00:13:26.610
The Bon Dance competition.

00:13:26.610 --> 00:13:28.450
The competition has a long history.

00:13:28.450 --> 00:13:31.300
Every year the winner gets a prize.

00:13:31.300 --> 00:13:35.300
By the way, our mistress was the 92nd winner.

00:13:35.300 --> 00:13:37.870
Really? Amazing, Yayoi-chan!

00:13:38.210 --> 00:13:40.410
Could you please teach Lion-san?

00:13:40.410 --> 00:13:43.300
What? I can already dance.

00:13:46.200 --> 00:13:49.450
I don't think we'll have time this 
year, but by next year I'll be sure to.

00:13:49.450 --> 00:13:52.050
Goodness gracious, isn't that good news?

00:13:54.000 --> 00:13:55.620
The train's here.

00:14:06.440 --> 00:14:09.270
This place is full of delicious food!

00:14:10.160 --> 00:14:11.220
Wait.

00:14:13.170 --> 00:14:14.620
Nina-chan?

00:14:15.540 --> 00:14:19.430
It would be bad if you got lost.

00:14:19.970 --> 00:14:21.210
Okay!

00:14:24.150 --> 00:14:25.600
Nina-chan, let's go!

00:14:26.260 --> 00:14:29.040
W-Wait, don't run.

00:14:46.130 --> 00:14:47.710
What's the matter?

00:14:47.710 --> 00:14:49.490
Do you want me to eat it for you?

00:14:50.300 --> 00:14:54.040
No. It's cute so I'm going 
to bring it home like this.

00:14:55.880 --> 00:14:58.160
Then would you like some cotton candy?

00:14:59.780 --> 00:15:01.070
It's good.

00:15:06.450 --> 00:15:08.050
It's sweet.

00:15:08.340 --> 00:15:10.040
See, it's good!

00:15:10.040 --> 00:15:11.170
Yeah.

00:15:11.170 --> 00:15:13.930
Lion-chan, Nina-chan.

00:15:14.770 --> 00:15:16.830
Let's have some takoyaki together.

00:15:17.820 --> 00:15:19.230
She's got takoyaki!

00:15:20.500 --> 00:15:22.310
You're getting a little overexcited.

00:15:22.930 --> 00:15:24.650
Now open wide.

00:15:26.910 --> 00:15:28.190
Delicious!

00:15:29.690 --> 00:15:32.620
Festivals are just so fun 
and delicious, aren't they?

00:15:32.620 --> 00:15:35.490
Now you too, Nina-chan.

00:15:37.290 --> 00:15:39.870
Lion-chan, have another.

00:15:42.300 --> 00:15:47.220
We've managed to have another splendid festival 
this year thanks to the Tachibana family support.

00:15:47.220 --> 00:15:49.010
Thank you very much.

00:15:49.460 --> 00:15:52.090
I'm honored to have been of service.

00:15:53.750 --> 00:15:56.020
It's about time for the competition to begin.

00:15:56.020 --> 00:15:56.820
Oh my.

00:15:56.820 --> 00:15:59.120
Ch-Ch-Ch-Chairwoman!

00:15:59.120 --> 00:16:00.480
What's the matter?

00:16:00.480 --> 00:16:03.520
The truth is, the winner's 
medal has disappeared.

00:16:06.210 --> 00:16:07.020
What's this?

00:16:08.730 --> 00:16:09.840
Bird feathers?

00:16:09.840 --> 00:16:12.000
They're everywhere!

00:16:12.000 --> 00:16:13.580
This is incomprehensible.

00:16:14.180 --> 00:16:19.010
We cannot let a Tachibana sponsored 
competition meet with such unfortunate events.

00:16:19.010 --> 00:16:20.040
Karin. Karen.

00:16:20.040 --> 00:16:21.770
Let's split up and look for the medal.

00:16:21.770 --> 00:16:23.420
Understood.
Roger!

00:16:21.770 --> 00:16:24.160
That's too much food, Nina-chan.

00:16:26.000 --> 00:16:27.290
Lion-san.

00:16:27.290 --> 00:16:28.490
What's the matter?

00:16:28.490 --> 00:16:29.750
Why are you in such a hurry?

00:16:30.280 --> 00:16:33.260
To tell you the truth, the prize 
for the competition has been stolen.

00:16:33.560 --> 00:16:36.210
We're in the middle of looking for it.

00:16:36.210 --> 00:16:39.130
Yayoi-chan, I'll help too.

00:16:39.950 --> 00:16:42.230
It's good to help one 
another in times of need.

00:16:42.230 --> 00:16:43.230
Mmhmm.

00:16:43.750 --> 00:16:48.060
I'm touched. All right then, 
I gladly accept your help!

00:16:51.770 --> 00:16:53.280
That's it!

00:16:53.560 --> 00:16:55.350
Everyone, look at that!

00:16:55.350 --> 00:16:58.240
These feathers were left 
all over the crime scene.

00:16:58.240 --> 00:17:02.420
That bird might have something 
to do with this feather.

00:17:02.420 --> 00:17:04.120
Score, score, score!

00:17:05.150 --> 00:17:06.780
A Foreigner response?

00:17:06.780 --> 00:17:08.920
Let's Trance to be on the safe side.

00:17:09.680 --> 00:17:12.550
Gate Access! Tetra-Heaven!

00:17:16.640 --> 00:17:18.960
Let's go, Michael.

00:17:20.100 --> 00:17:23.380
<i>Use my power as much as you need.</i>

00:17:36.620 --> 00:17:39.450
Gate Access! Disfia!

00:17:41.410 --> 00:17:44.100
Let's do whatever it takes 
to find that medal, Qipao.

00:17:44.100 --> 00:17:46.790
<i>I see you need my power.</i>

00:18:07.860 --> 00:18:09.260
Wha?

00:18:09.260 --> 00:18:11.610
What happened to that Foreigner response?

00:18:11.610 --> 00:18:13.820
No good! There's no response!

00:18:20.950 --> 00:18:22.540
Could it be?

00:18:23.040 --> 00:18:23.830
I knew it.

00:18:26.080 --> 00:18:28.610
Is this the medal you were looking for?

00:18:28.610 --> 00:18:32.290
T-That's it! Good job, Nina-san!

00:18:32.290 --> 00:18:37.380
Mistress, now the Bon Dance can
continue without interruption!

00:18:37.380 --> 00:18:38.390
Medal?

00:18:38.390 --> 00:18:39.380
Yay!

00:18:39.940 --> 00:18:41.400
Goodness gracious.

00:18:43.300 --> 00:18:44.000
Uh-oh.

00:18:45.280 --> 00:18:46.540
<i>Yuko'll find me!</i>

00:18:46.540 --> 00:18:49.760
It's the president! 
What are you doing up there?

00:18:49.760 --> 00:18:52.000
<i>D-Don't come any closer!</i>

00:18:52.000 --> 00:18:54.320
Huh? What are you doing?

00:18:54.660 --> 00:18:56.360
Up we go.

00:18:56.910 --> 00:18:58.240
<i>Shoo! Shoo!</i>

00:18:58.670 --> 00:19:00.700
What?

00:19:06.810 --> 00:19:09.470
Nina-san? What's the matter?

00:19:10.480 --> 00:19:11.960
I really can't tell you.

00:19:12.290 --> 00:19:14.210
What brought this attitude on?

00:19:14.500 --> 00:19:17.370
By the way, Nina, your face is all red.

00:19:17.370 --> 00:19:19.220
Don't worry about me.

00:19:19.220 --> 00:19:21.010
Hurry up and do something about Lion-san!

00:19:21.010 --> 00:19:23.090
What's the matter with Lion-san?

00:19:23.090 --> 00:19:26.530
Now that you mention her, where is she?

00:19:26.530 --> 00:19:28.100
She's all the way up there?!

00:19:28.100 --> 00:19:29.600
No! You can't go!

00:19:31.460 --> 00:19:33.590
Gosh! What is going on?

00:19:35.090 --> 00:19:37.360
It's about what's under her yukata.

00:19:38.430 --> 00:19:39.980
Mumble mumble mumble...

00:19:41.200 --> 00:19:43.640
Buck naked!

00:19:46.610 --> 00:19:48.950
How could this have happened?

00:19:49.450 --> 00:19:53.960
It's true that traditionally Japanese women 
didn't wear anything under their kimonos.

00:19:54.530 --> 00:19:57.570
But Lion-san would never be aware of such a—

00:19:57.570 --> 00:20:00.840
Wait, the one who helped 
Lion put on her yukata?

00:20:01.280 --> 00:20:04.890
It's normal not to wear underwear 
under a yukata. Right?

00:20:05.570 --> 00:20:06.600
No way.

00:20:06.860 --> 00:20:08.720
Wait, then you too?

00:20:08.720 --> 00:20:10.050
Buck naked!

00:20:10.050 --> 00:20:10.850
Karen!

00:20:10.850 --> 00:20:13.140
Oh, no! The president needs help!

00:20:13.410 --> 00:20:16.120
L-Lion-san, be more careful with your legs!

00:20:16.120 --> 00:20:17.880
Come down right now!

00:20:19.480 --> 00:20:21.040
I'd expect nothing less, Yuko.

00:20:27.740 --> 00:20:30.750
Pirari Town Bon Odori Dance Competition

00:20:59.990 --> 00:21:02.190
Nina-chan, come dance with us!

00:21:07.940 --> 00:21:09.620
Nina-chan, let's dance.

00:21:10.320 --> 00:21:13.010
But I said I'm fine.

00:21:13.010 --> 00:21:14.820
Japan has an old saying.

00:21:14.820 --> 00:21:18.790
"You're a fool if you dance, and 
a fool if you just look on."

00:21:18.790 --> 00:21:20.210
If you're going to be a fool either way,

00:21:20.210 --> 00:21:22.130
the one who has more fun is the winner.

00:21:31.900 --> 00:21:33.860
I guess I have no choice.

00:21:36.610 --> 00:21:39.650
I wanted to have a yukata date.

00:21:40.520 --> 00:21:42.680
It's our last summer break 
together and everything.

00:21:47.270 --> 00:21:48.830
Yuko!

00:21:53.310 --> 00:21:56.670
We used to eat these all the 
time when we were little.

00:21:56.670 --> 00:21:57.670
Yeah.

00:21:59.060 --> 00:22:00.790
You know what, Mizuki?

00:22:02.370 --> 00:22:04.630
It's about what we were 
talking about yesterday.

00:22:04.630 --> 00:22:08.930
I find myself having the most fun when I'm 
looking after Lion-chan and her friends.

00:22:10.060 --> 00:22:12.170
When I see their smiling faces,

00:22:12.170 --> 00:22:14.890
I feel happy from the bottom of my heart.

00:22:15.840 --> 00:22:16.900
If it's at all possible,

00:22:16.900 --> 00:22:22.440
I'd like to watch over all 
of them as they grow older.

00:22:23.090 --> 00:22:26.030
I guess. You can't really 
call that a dream, can you?

00:22:27.630 --> 00:22:28.960
No.

00:22:28.960 --> 00:22:31.030
I think it's a splendid dream.

00:22:33.300 --> 00:22:35.200
Thanks, Mizuki.

00:22:37.190 --> 00:22:39.450
Look. It's Lion-chan and her friends.

00:22:41.950 --> 00:22:43.330
Jeez.

00:22:43.330 --> 00:22:46.360
Lion-san. Don't run around so wildly!

00:22:44.800 --> 00:22:46.360
Everyone will see!

00:22:46.960 --> 00:22:49.970
Episode 7 
You're a Hina if You Dance, 
And a President if You Just Look On

00:22:51.650 --> 00:22:53.890
Looks like this year's summer 
break is coming to a close.

00:22:54.210 --> 00:22:55.760
Yup.

00:22:55.760 --> 00:22:57.040
You don't sound very satisfied.

00:22:57.400 --> 00:23:00.400
There were so many things I wanted to 
do that I couldn't that it's depressing.

00:23:00.670 --> 00:23:05.390
I couldn't go to the beach, or the 
hot springs, or see any fireworks.

00:23:05.390 --> 00:23:07.390
I feel like we had the same 
conversation last year.

00:23:07.390 --> 00:23:08.940
The most depressing thing is how

00:23:08.940 --> 00:23:13.800
people think teachers get the same 
kind of summer break as students.

00:23:14.300 --> 00:23:17.160
We have to make the curriculum for the 
second semester and go to training courses.

00:23:17.160 --> 00:23:21.350
Our schedules are so packed that summer 
break is actually busier than the school year.

00:23:21.970 --> 00:23:23.170
That's true.

00:23:24.320 --> 00:23:27.350
I even got a new bathing suit this year.

00:23:29.150 --> 00:23:30.960
Do you want to go our next day off?

00:23:30.960 --> 00:23:32.390
Really?!

00:23:32.390 --> 00:23:35.920
I do! Yay! My first trip 
to the beach this year!

00:23:36.770 --> 00:23:39.310
You're pretty simpleminded, aren't you?
